=== CI provisioning rehearsal (proactive, before opening the PR, per the lesson from OCOR-DEV-0017/0018): OPA, Keycloak and OpenBao are all pre-built pinned images (unlike Fuseki), so a docker run recipe was rehearsed on alternate host ports (8182/8081/8201) before adding it to the 3 CI workflows ===
docker run openpolicyagent/opa@sha256:39daf... run --server --addr 0.0.0.0:8181 -> became healthy (curl /health -> {}) within seconds
docker run quay.io/openbao/openbao@sha256:11fd73a... server -dev -dev-listen-address=0.0.0.0:8200 -> became healthy (curl /v1/sys/health -> initialized:true, sealed:false) within seconds
docker run quay.io/keycloak/keycloak@sha256:9d1f1b2... start-dev --http-port=8080 -> became healthy (curl /realms/master/.well-known/openid-configuration -> real OIDC discovery document) within ~20-30s (the slowest of the three, as expected)
cleanup: docker rm -f opa-ci-test openbao-ci-test keycloak-ci-test -- the live ocor-bootstrap stack (11 services) was confirmed unaffected before and after

